{
  "case_id": "2017-16-712",
  "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Allyson N. Ho",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HO: Yes, certainly, Justice Ginsburg. And -- and our position -- our position is not that the PTO is precluded from error correction. It simply can't do it through this adjudication. So, for example, we believe ex parte reexams, which are fundamentally examinational and not adjudicational in nature, are perfectly consistent with Article III."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Why not -- why not, though, Ms. Ho, just simply say the question is whether there's a private right involved?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ho",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We certainly do stake our ground on that it's a private right. We think this Court held -- has held as much already in Horne."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ho",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Privy Council revoked its last patent in -- in any -- any case, ordinary or otherwise, in -- in 1779."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kise",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the panel packing, if you will, mentioned by Petitioner in the briefs, I don't believe -- and -- and I'll leave it to the government to -- to have the exact statistics -- precise statistics, but I don't believe that that's taken place more than one or two times, and I don't believe it's taken place with respect -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first is that this can't be done by executive branch officials because the effect of patent cancellation is to take away a private property interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Well, to go directly to your question about public employees, because I think it is a good analogy, the Court has said that if a public employee has tenure protection, a guarantee that he or she can be fired only for cause, then the employee has a property right in this job"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Does it comport to due process to change the composition of the adjudicatory body halfway through the proceeding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f53ef8517b11-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I guess that would be unconstitutional, too?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-712",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "f53ef8517b11ce312544b4d6eaa133a457eacbd6e6973b272d08ba68b6f1cede",
